// <cmath> - The floating-point functions, under `std::`.
//
// C++ overloads each of these for `float` and `long double` as well. This does
// not: `lib/math.h` declares the `double` form alone, so `std::sqrt(2.0f)`
// converts to double and back rather than calling `sqrtf`. The answer is the
// same one; the call is not the one a conforming library would make.
//
// Derived from lib/math.h: every name that header declares is named here, and
// the two are checked against each other by the case that includes both.
